ural shift, the existing Receipt endpoint in Altinn 2 can no longer be used to access receipts for the Broker service, as those records do not exist in that environment anymore [1]. If continued use of this specific endpoint is required, consumers/service owners must submit a feature request with detailed examples so it can be evaluated [1].\n\n**Virus Scanning**\n- The provided documentation does not mention virus scanning or any changes related to malware/content verification as part of the Altinn 2 Broker transition to Altinn 3 [1][2]. \n\n**Other Notable Impacts for Consumers/Service Owners**\n- File availability: Files transferred via this broker flow will remain available in both Altinn 2 and Altinn 3 environments [1]. \n- Size limits: A maximum file size of 1 GB still applies, as it is the hard limit enforced by Altinn 2; consequently, the corresponding Altinn 3 Resource must be configured with this same restriction [1].\n- Request routing: For calls that explicitly specify `ServiceCode`/`ServiceEdition`, requests are immediately routed to Altinn 3 via the Broker Bridge [1]. If those fields are not specified, a fallback call is first made to Altinn 2 storage before querying Altinn 3 [1].\n- Manifest files: The use of Manifest files in submitted file data is deprecated by default within this transition solution, though functionality can be explicitly enabled if required [1].\n\n*Note on source coverage:* While the context thoroughly details the receipt handling and architectural routing changes, it does not provide information regarding virus scanning or related security processing during the migration. All claims above are drawn directly from sources [1] and [2].", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? false, :question-id "ue-broker-04-overgang-a2-a3-forskjeller", :empty? false, :llm-calls 2, :citation-recall 0.0, :completion-tokens 478, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 0.0, :config-id "enriched-hq", :clari