app instance metadata endpoint | list all app instances filtering | instance fetching get post put delete", :timestamp "2026-06-11T16:00:03.565612Z", :total-tokens 8202, :run-id "de9d4675-46b0-42a7-b6ee-ccfeefb93e62", :golden-display-rank 2, :steps-executed 3, :dataset "public-docs", :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 0.0} {:response "Based on the provided context, there is **no information** regarding a `POST /app` endpoint or its authentication and request body requirements for publishing App events [2]. \n\nThe text explicitly distinguishes between generic API event publishing and how Altinn App events work:\n\n🔹 **If you meant the documented `POST /events` endpoint:**\n- **Authentication:** Requires the Maskinporten scope `altinn:events.publish` [1].\n- **Request Body Content Type:** Must be set to `application/cloudevents+json` [1].\n- **Body Structure:** The body must contain a Cloud Event serialized as a JSON string. Accepted properties include the event ID (string), event type (string), event source (URI URI), resource ID, instance ID, and an alternative subject identifier (e.g., `/person/[id]` or `/organisation/[id]) [1]. It also accepts all standard Cloud Event v1.02 spec attributes plus custom extension keys are accepted as well [1].\n⚠️ *Note:* Source [1] explicitly states that `POST /events is for *\"generic events - events that are not strictly Altinn Studio App events\"* [1]].\n\n🔹 **Regarding actual \"Altinn App events\":**\nSource [2 explains that publishing these events **\"is handled by core logic in the application\"** rather than via a direct API call like `POST /app`. Developers are directed to consult separate Altinn Apps documentation to enable the functionality and define custom events, meaning no endpoint/authentication/request body specs for `/app` are provided here.\n\nIf you intended `POST /events`, use the Maskinporten scope & CloudEvents JSON payload above [1]. If you specifically need App event scopes/structures, they fall outside this context and require reviewing core application logic or a different documentation set", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? false, :question-id "ue-api-05-events-post-app-token", :empty? false, :llm-calls 3, :citation-recall 0.0, :completion-tokens 456, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 0.0, :config-id "enriched-hq", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "altinn-3-general,hard", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features nil, :response-chars 1733, :source "new", :search-passes 1, :n-retrieved 2, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? false, :golden-pool-rank nil, :golden-read? false, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? true, :retrieved-chunk-ids "aa953fcdd337;03f0f1c41d4c", :enrichment-hits 31, :n-expected 2, :status "complete", :recall-at-20 0.0, :refinement-corpus-grounded? nil, :n-cited 2, :prompt-tokens 7859, :pool-head "", :repeat 0, :error nil, :cited-chunk-ids "aa953fcdd337;03f0f1c41d4c", :expected-chunk-ids "eab508bca469;bdf5fc355e77", :elapsed-ms 213226, :issued-queries "altinn publish event endpoint app API request body parameters | Postman altinn createEventAltinn3 event post payload required fields authentication", :timestamp "2026-06-11T16:03:17.349492Z", :total-tokens 8315, :run-id "32492de6-ca64-4328-a81c-b9a697b394c0", :golden-display-rank nil, :steps-executed 3, :dataset "public-docs", :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 0.0} {:response "Based on the provided context:\n\n**Authentication:**\nFor `POST /app`, authentication requires both a Platform Access token and an Altinn token, which must be inserted into the request headers as follows:\n- Header: `PlatformAccessToken: {Sett inn Platform Access token}` \n- Header: `Authorization: Bearer {Sett inn Altinn token}` [2]\n\n**Request Body:**\nThe body should contain a JSON object representing the cloud event. Based on the provided `/app` example, it must include standard Cloud Event fields such as `\"type\"` (e.g., `\"app.instance.created\"`), `\"source\"`, `\"subject\"`, and `\"specversion\"` (e.g., `\"1.0\"`). It can also optionally contain an `\"alternativesubject\"` to provide a subscriber-friendly identifier [2].\n\n**Note on ambiguity/endpoint distinction:**\nThe context explicitly differentiates between two endpoints with separate authentication and payload requirements:\n- `POST /events` is intended for generic events and requires the Maskinporten scope `altinn:events.publish`, while also noting that its content type differs from app events [1]. \n- `/app` (as shown in the curl example) uses Platform Access + Altinn tokens instead of a Maskinporten scope, and follows the JSON structure detailed above [2]. \n\nEnsure you align your implementation with the specific endpoint path your integration targets to avoid credential or format mismatches.", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? false, :question-id "ue-api-05-events-post-app-token", :empty? false, :llm-calls 3, :citation-recall 0.0, :completion-tokens 294, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 0.0, :config-id "off", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "altinn-3-general,hard", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features nil, :response-chars 1357, :source "new", :search-passes 1, :n-retrieved 2, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? false, :golden-pool-rank nil, :golden-read? false, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? true, :retrieved-chunk-ids "aa953fcdd337;b93dfb54f9b7", :enrichment-hits 0, :n-expected 2, :status "complete", :recall-at-20 0.0, :refinement-corpus-grounded? nil, :n-cited 2, :prompt-tokens 7851, :pool-head "", :repeat 1, :error nil, :cited-chunk-ids "aa953fcdd337;b93dfb54f9b7", :expected-chunk-ids "eab508bca469;bdf5fc355e77", :elapsed-ms 237981, :issued-queries "post /app/events altinn documentation api publication | /app/event endpoints publishing events authentication bearer token", :timestamp "2026-06-11T16:04:01.548866Z", :total-tokens 8145, :run-id "37efc384-83fb-4d95-a409-b6acc8c01d0d", :golden-display-rank nil, :steps-executed 3, :dataset "public-docs", :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 0.0} {:response "Based on the provided context, here are the requirements for publishing an app event via the `POST /app` endpoint:\n\n**Authentication**\nThe API explicitly requires authentication with a `Platform Access Token` included in the header [1]. Additionally, the curl example demonstrates that you must also include your Altinn token using the standard authorization format (`Authorization: Bearer {Insert Altinn token}`) when calling this specific route [2]. The request headers should specify both tokens alongside an appropriate content type.\n\n**Request Body**\nThe body must be formatted as `application/json` and should contain the cloud event data, typically structured according to the [`AppCloudEventRequestModel`](https://github.com/Altinn/altinn-events/blob/main/src/Events/Models/AppCloudEventRequestModel.cs) [1]. According to the documentation, the payload should include:\n- `type`: A string representing the event type of the cloud event.\n- `source`: The event source as a URI.\n- `subject` (party ID): The party ID for the instanceOwner as a string, formatted as `_ /party/{partyId} _`. \n- `specversion`: The Cloud Event spec version as a string [1]. *(Note: Example payloads use `\"specversion\": \"1.0\"`)*.\n- `alternativesubject` (optional but recommended): An alternative identifier for the subject as a string, commonly known to your subscribers (e.g., `/person/{pid}` or `/organisation/{orgno}`). The documentation advises including this property if the main `subject` contains an internal ID unknown to event subscribers [1].\n\nAdditionally, you do not need to manually provide the `id` and `time` fields in the request body, as the Events service will automatically set them on the cloud event during processing [1].", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true,