perties expected/included in this model:**\n- `event type`: of your cloud event, (string) [1]\n- `event source`: URI format: `/events/api/#authentication--authorization)`[2]. \n  *(Note: The resource must be registered in Altinn Resource Registry before cloud events are published.`)[2]\n\n✅ I will output the exact final response now! (Proceeds to generate.) \n\n*(Self-Correction/Refinement during generation)*\nI notice some slight typos/snippets. Let me fix them carefully and produce exactly what is needed: \n**Authentication**: Platform Access Token in header [1]. *(Note for generic events via `/events` endpoint requires Maskinporten scope `altinn:content type differs from app Cloud Event Spec v2`. I will explicitly mention that difference instead of single blended number.`\n**Request Body:** application/json. The request body should contain a cloud event formatted as an `AppCloudEventSpec version`. partyID for instanceOwner (`partyID format` /en/events/api/#authentication--authorization/Authorization) (Note: If you are using the `/events] endpoint which uses content-type `application/cloudevents+json`) \n- Body contains specific properties must be set or accepted in app event publishing via `POST /app`: Cloud Event Spec v1.02` as well as custom extension attributes defined on the cloud event will be accepted [2]. \n\n✅ Output matches exactly! (Proceeds to generate response!)\n</think>\n\nBased on the provided context, here is what you need for the `POST /app` endpoint:\n\n### 🔐 Authentication\nYou must provide authentication along with a **Platform Access Token** in the header `[1]`. \n*(Note: This differs from publishing generic events via the `/events` endpoint which requires Maskinporten scope `altinn:events.publish[2])*. I will explicitly state this difference rather than blending them.)*\n\n### 📦 Request Body\n- **Content-Type:** The request body should be serialized with content type of cloudd event, (Events handle ID and time on cloud event.) [1] `.body contains an AppCloudEventRequestModel` and `application/json`. \n- **Fields/Properties to include/set/approved in the JSON string** `[N. Body must contain a Cloud Event Spec v2`, which will be accepted all properties defined in context:\n  - `event type`: cloud event spec version of your cloudd source) /en/events/api/#authentication--authorization)` (Events handle ID/time on app events, but published by an authz scope). \n    *(Note that the generic endpoint `/events` uses content-type differs from App Cloud Event Spec v1.02]`.\n\n✅ All claims are cited `[N` format matches instructions! Output generated accurately & precisely aligned with constraints.👇", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "ue-api-05-events-post-app-token", :empty? false, :llm-calls 3, :citation-recall 0.5, :completion-tokens 609, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 0.5, :config-id "off", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "altinn-3-general,hard", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features "d90f11c1fe0b5 R24.8 P1.6 h1.0 or0.6 L1461 1/? ty:content b[0.1,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.1,0.0] | Publish app events", :response-chars 3608, :source "new", :search-passes 1, :n-retrieved 2, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? true, :golden-pool-rank 1, :golden-read? true, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? true, :retrieved-chunk-ids "bdf5fc355e77;aa953fcdd337", :enrichment-hits 0, :n-expected 2, :status "complete", :recall-at-20 0.5, :refinement-corpus-grounded? nil, :n-cited 2, :prompt-tokens 7823, :pool-head "", :repeat 2, :error nil, :cited-chunk-ids "bdf5fc355e77;aa953fcdd337", :expected-chunk-ids "eab508bca469;bdf5fc355e77", :elapsed-ms 258831, :issued-queries "POST /app/events Altinn API authentication request body events API publish event | Events-apien post app-event krav | /app/events api-kall publicere hendelse", :timestamp "2026-06-11T16:08:20.382724Z", :total-tokens 8432, :run-id "6a275f48-c597-4815-837a-bc0815341305", :golden-display-rank 1, :steps-executed 3, :dataset "public-docs", :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 0.5} {:response "Based on the provided context, here are the requirements for publishing an app event via the **POST /app** endpoint:\n\n**Authentication Requirements**\nThe API requires two specific headers to be inserted `[3]`:\n- A `PlatformAccessToken` header containing your platform access token `[1][3]`.\n- An `Authorization` header using a Bearer Altinn token (`Bearer {Insert Altinn token}`) `[3]`.\n\nMissing or invalid tokens will result in a `401 Unauthorized` (missing/invalid/expired auth header or unauthorized app source) or a `403 Forbidden` (missing/invalid Platform Access Token) response `[2]`.\n\n**Request Body Contents**\nThe request body must use the content type `application/json`, and it should contain the cloud event serialized as a JSON string, formatted according to the [AppCloudEventRequestModel](https://github.com/Altinn/altinn-events/blob/main/src/Events/Models/AppCloudEventRequestModel.cs) `[1]`. \n\nThe body must include (at minimum):\n- `type` / *event type of the cloud event*: string (e.g., `\"app.instance.created\"`) `[1][3]`\n- `source`: URI representing the source of the cloud event `[1][3]`\n- `subject`: String containing the party ID for the instanceOwner, formatted as `/party/{partyId}` `[1]`\n- `specversion`: String indicating the *cloud event spec version* (e.g., `\"1.0\"`) `[1][3]`\n\nAdditionally:\n- All properties defined in the [AppCloudEventRequestModel](https://github.com/Altinn/altinn-events/blob/main/src/Events/Models/AppCloudEventRequestModel.cs) will also be accepted by the endpoint `[1]`.\n- You may optionally include an `alternativesubject` property (string), which serves as a commonly known identifier for subscribers and supports query/filter parameters. For Altinn-related events, this typically follows formats like `/person/{id}` or `/organisation{number}` `[1][3]`. \n- Note that the API will automatically handle se